            <ArticleTitle>Intracranial haemophilic pseudotumor associated with factor VIII deficiency.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>455-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/02688690902774754</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Haemophilic pseudotumor is a rare complication of haemophilia occurring in 1-2% of patients and is more frequently located is in the long bones of the lower extremities and in the pelvis. We present the first case of an intracranial haemophilic pseudotumor in a patient with factor VIII deficiency.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
